  {
    "id": 83881,
    "name": "Unix Shells",
    "visible": 1,
    "summary": "<p dir=\"ltr\">The main goal of this part of the lecture is to make you familiar with the usage of the shell. This reflects the following content:</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n    <li><a href=\"https://linuxcommand.org/tlcl.php\" title=\"https://linuxcommand.org/tlcl.php\">The Linux Command Line - A Complete Introduction (by William Shotts)</a>&nbsp;(TLCL)<br>It is especially \"Part 1: Learning the Shell\" which we consider as essential skill to work with any unixoide operating system</li>\r\n    <li><a href=\"https://pages.itplus.fh-joanneum.at/t00000/dme/\" title=\"https://pages.itplus.fh-joanneum.at/t00000/dme/\">Data Meets Engineering</a>&nbsp;(DME)<br>Additionally we have started to collect some hints and input regarding Linux on above page. This page will potentially grow and has the purpose to cover topics which are especially true for setups you will see here at FH JOANNEUM.</li>\r\n</ul>Additionally I will share files and information with you which are dedicated to this years lecture inside a git repository:<p></p><p></p><ul><li>https://gitlab.itplus.fh-joanneum.at/study/dat/dat26w/courses/rul/course-ws-2627<br></li></ul><p></p>",
