  {
    "id": 83882,
    "name": "Learning The Shell - Part 1",
    "visible": 1,
    "summary": "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">We will cover the following topics</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\"></p><ul><li>DME |&nbsp;<a href=\"https://pages.itplus.fh-joanneum.at/t00000/dme/linux/remote/#openssh\" title=\"https://pages.itplus.fh-joanneum.at/t00000/dme/linux/remote/#openssh\">OpenSSH</a>: Login to remove VM</li><li>TLCL | Chapter 1: What is the Shell?</li><li>TLCL | Chapter 2: Navigation</li><li>TLCL | Chapter 3: Exploring the System (see also <a href=\"https://pages.itplus.fh-joanneum.at/t00000/dme/linux/fs/\" title=\"https://pages.itplus.fh-joanneum.at/t00000/dme/linux/fs/\">DME | Unix System V Structure</a>)</li><li>TLCL | Chapter 4: Manipulating Files and Directories</li><li>TLCL | Chapter 5:&nbsp;Working with Commands</li><li>TLCL | Chapter 9: Permissions</li></ul><p><br></p><p>The connection command (to login on your virtual machine):</p><pre>ssh &lt;username&gt;@ca-crs-dat-&lt;id&gt;.itplus.fh-joanneum.at</pre><div class=\"attostylesbox attostylesbox-outline attostylesbox-outline-information\">Attention: You need to be connected via VPN if you are not within FHJ network (e.g. FHJ WiFi)</div><p></p>",
